/* ============================================================================
 * Fire Babys — Sitewide Language System (i18n.js)
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Jeff's order (2026-10-17): "let the world choose what language they want
 * the game to be in — add in every language possible to choose from."
 * Upgraded same day: "do what every other game does" — ALL text translates
 * and re-renders on switch, including canvas-drawn text.
 *
 * HOW IT WORKS (the industry string-table pattern, without editing games):
 *   1. A 🌐 picker button sits on EVERY page. The chosen language is saved
 *      to localStorage ("fb_lang"); first visit auto-detects the browser
 *      language, else English.
 *   2. DOM text: a walker translates text nodes + title/placeholder/
 *      aria-label attributes from a dictionary of the site's real UI
 *      strings, and a MutationObserver re-applies it to anything games
 *      add later (HUD updates, briefing screens, win/lose banners, the
 *      sign-in gate's own messages — all live in the same DOM).
 *   3. Canvas text: CanvasRenderingContext2D.fillText / strokeText /
 *      measureText are patched so any string a game draws is looked up in
 *      the same dictionary first. Games redraw every frame, so a language
 *      switch takes effect on the next frame — exactly like a string
 *      table re-render.
 *   4. Numbers inside labels ("Score: 120", "LEVEL 3/10") are handled by
 *      pattern templates per language.
 *
 * SAFETY RULES BAKED IN
 *   - Character names and brands are NEVER translated (Blaze, Aqua,
 *     Sparky, Ruko, Boulder, Sizzle, Cinder, Pebble, Drift, Bubble,
 *     Splash, Pyra, Lord Inferno, Lord Tidal, "Fire Babys", "Fire World").
 *   - Numbers-only / emoji-only / single-glyph strings are never touched.
 *   - Originals are stored, so switching back to English restores the
 *     page exactly.
 *   - No external images or requests: emoji + CSS + JS only, so the
 *     strict 3d.html CSP is honoured.
 *   - Everything is wrapped so a failure here can never break a page:
 *     if i18n fails, the site runs exactly as before, in English.
 *
 * Loaded site-wide by auth-gate.js (every page already includes the gate).
 * ========================================================================== */
